.TH CRAM 1 "November 2026" "cram 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cram \- track your study hours from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cram
.br
.B cram start
.RI [ class ]
.br
.B cram stop
.br
.B cram log
.RI [ class ] " text"
.br
.B cram add
.BR details | memo | block
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B cram edit block
.br
.B cram create class
.I name
.br
.BR "cram ls\-class" " | " "cram ls\-log" " | " "cram ls\-memo"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cram
logs study blocks: when you studied, for which class, and what you covered.
Run
.B cram
on its own for the full-screen app, which also has the day and week views, editing, notes and settings.
Everything is saved the moment it changes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR start " [\fIclass\fR [\fIdetails\fR...]] [\fB\-\-at\fR \fItime\fR]"
Start a block. The class can be shortened (\fBstat\fR for Statics). With no class, cram asks which one,
or for a new class name if you have none. A name that isn't a class yet: cram offers to create it.
.TP
.BR stop " [\fB\-\-at\fR \fItime\fR]"
Stop the current block.
.TP
.BI "add details " text
Add details to the block you're in.
.TP
.BR log " [\fIclass\fR] \fItext\fR"
Log what you did for a class: what you finished, what's still shaky. While you're studying, leave the class out
and it goes to the class you're in.
.TP
.BR "add memo" " [\fB\-c\fR \fIclass\fR] \fItext\fR"
Put a memo on the memo board. Tag it with a class by starting it with the class and a colon
(\fBstatics: review slides\fR) or with \fB\-c\fR. There are no reminders. Check memos off in the app.
.TP
.B add block
Log a past block you forgot to start. Asks the class, the day, the start and end times, and optional details.
.TP
.BR "edit block" " [\fB\-\-date\fR \fIday\fR] [\fB\-\-start\fR \fItime\fR] [\fB\-\-end\fR \fItime\fR] [\fB\-\-details\fR \fItext\fR]... [\fB\-c\fR \fIclass\fR]"
Pick a block from today or another day this week, then choose to edit its time, its details or its class.
Each value is shown already typed in, ready to change; clear a line of details to remove it.
A block from today keeps its date. If the new times overlap another block, cram offers to merge them,
fit this one into the gap, shorten the other, replace it, or change the times again.
Plain \fBcram edit\fR does the same.
.TP
.BI "create class " name
Create a class. Separate several with commas: \fBcram create class Statics, Calc III\fR.
.TP
.B ls\-class
Your classes, with hours this week, in total, and when you last studied each.
.TP
.BR ls\-log " [\fIclass\fR]"
One class's log, newest first, or every class's log grouped by class.
.TP
.B ls\-memo
The memo board: this week's memos, plus any left open from earlier weeks.
.PP
Times accept \fB9\fR, \fB9am\fR, \fB9:30pm\fR, \fB21:30\fR, \fBnoon\fR; days accept \fBtoday\fR,
\fByesterday\fR, weekday names, \fB10/14\fR and \fB2026\-10\-14\fR.
.SH THE APP
The bottom bar takes the same words as the shell: \fBstart\fR [\fIclass\fR], \fBstop\fR,
\fBlog\fR, \fBadd details\fR, \fBadd memo\fR, \fBadd block\fR, \fBcreate class\fR, plus \fBundo\fR and \fBredo\fR.
Type \fB/\fR for views: \fB/day\fR, \fB/week\fR, \fB/log\fR, \fB/memo\fR, \fB/classes\fR, \fB/config\fR.
\fBtab\fR moves between the bottom bar and the panels; arrow keys move between panels and \fBenter\fR opens one.
\fBctrl+s\fR starts or stops, \fBctrl+z\fR undoes, \fBf1\fR lists every key, \fBctrl+q\fR quits.
.SH TAB COMPLETION
Run \fBcram \-\-install\-completion\fR once and open a new terminal. Tab then completes commands and class names.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cram/config.toml
Theme, banner and mascot settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cram/data.json
Your blocks, classes, log and memos. \fIdata.json.bak\fR is the previous version; a damaged file is replaced by it automatically.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRAM_HOME
Keep config and data in this one folder instead.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cram create class Statics, Calc III
cram start statics
cram add details "ch 5 problems"
cram stop
cram log statics "moments still shaky"
cram add memo "email the TA"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/ricozama121803/cram
